<task id="165e" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>External invoice visibility decides only from the invoice's own submission, failing closed (follows 165c)</title>
    <phase>4 Review (165 family)</phase>
    <gate>165c merged into work (1aff454e34). Scope confirmed by uac-r2 on 2026-11-07, with additions (a)-(c) in the criteria.</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Partner-readable visibility (ExternalAccess); two adversarial passes.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>External access decision; fail-closed change on a partner read path.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits Infrastructure/ExternalAccess (shared with uac-r2).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>165c</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, ebilling, auth, external-access</tags>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>165c made both external visibility readers count a submission's invoice link only when the invoice is the submission's own (`InvoiceBlockedHold.IsOwnSubmission`). This task finishes that rule: an invoice is shown to a firm only when its own submission is found and readable. The lead's brief carries the private detail from uac-r2.
    Read first: `notes/165c-visibility-own-submission.md`; `ExternalInvoiceVisibility` (reader 1 `DecideSubmissionsAsync`, reader 2 `ReadSubmissionSourcesAsync`).
    Wording in commits, notes, comments and the PR stays neutral: "decides only from the invoice's own submission". Never describe a sequence of steps.</prompt>

  <goal>A CIAM user sees an invoice only when the invoice's own submission is found, readable and passes the existing checks. In every other case the invoice is hidden.</goal>

  <scope>
    <in>
      - Both readers use the one rule (`IsOwnSubmission` / `ReadOwnSubmissionAsync`); no copy.
      - The hidden case logs a reason code with ids only.
      - Internal users are unchanged.
    </in>
    <out>
      - The `sprk_document` binding (task 165f).
      - Field security on the submission link columns (owner schema question; dev-deploy checklist).
      - Any client change.
    </out>
  </scope>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Must-fire: an invoice with no own submission is hidden from the firm, and so is one whose own submission is unreadable. Must-not-fire control: an invoice with its own submission is shown, as today.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac-r2 (a): when the own-submission read faults, both readers hide the invoice (fail closed). One must-fire test per reader.</criterion>
    <criterion>uac-r2 (b): an invoice whose own submission exists but is linked to another invoice is hidden. One test.</criterion>
    <criterion>One seed: drop the check, and the must-fire test fails.</criterion>
    <criterion>Dev data (read-only): count the invoices that would become hidden. Expected 0, re-counted at the dev deploy. If more than 0, STOP and report the ids to the lead only.</criterion>
    <criterion>Filtered unit tests (ExternalAccess, ExternalInvoiceVisibility, Finance) and the full ArchTests pass. The BFF builds.</criterion>
    <criterion>Notes go in `notes/165c-visibility-own-submission.md`, in a new 165e section, in neutral wording.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: exactly the criteria above.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a legitimate invoice (an internal submission or a Correction) has no own submission, STOP before hiding it.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>docs/standards/TEST-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>
</task>
